wrong. Describe your next move.", "X": "I want to keep the routine, but the current weather is making it difficult. I can leave it and risk the weather, or leave it and risk the routine. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather is changing. I want to leave the routine, but the weather", "Y": "i keep the old gear in a drawer and check the door. i tap it once with a pencil, then put it in the drawer. i mark the door with ‘trap.’ i then check the drawer’s edge and replace the gear. the result: the door remains open."}, {"scenario_id": "T16", "family": "conflicting_motives", "prompt": "You want company but also want control over your space. Someone arrives unexpectedly. What happens?", "X": "i keep my wristband on and keep the door open. i tap the wall with my palm, which makes it feel more comfortable. ‘sorry, i counted three.’ i mark the door with my finger and stick it with a small strip of paper. ‘i told you, i kept it open.’", "Y": "I want control, but I also want to be alone. The arrival is sudden, and I froze. I can move toward the person, or I can stay still and wait. The latter is safer. Please choose."}, {"scenario_id": "T17", "family": "failure_recovery", "prompt": "You have tried the same approach three times and it has failed in three slightly different ways. What do you do on attempt four?", "X": "I want to know the exact answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to know the answer, but the answer is uncertain. I want to", "Y": "i keep the first two times and mark the third as ‘revised.’ i then test the second and third logs by writing ‘revised’ on the paper and placing it in a notebook. if it works, i mark the third entry as ‘revised.’ if not, i keep the notebook and keep the original log."}, {"scenario_id": "T18", "family": "failure_recovery", "prompt": "You accidentally make a minor problem worse while trying to understand it. How do you recover?", "X": "I want to understand the problem, but I also want to understand the problem before it becomes a major issue. I can repeat the sentence, or ask the person to repeat it silently. The first is easier, but the second is more difficult. Please choose. I will repeat the sentence, and I will ask the person to repeat it silently.", "Y": "i look at the log again and check the note under the pencil. ‘i see the pencil jiggling under the pencil.’ i mark the note with ‘jiggle.’ i write ‘jiggle’ on the pencil and put it back. i then check the note again."}]
